CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ common comparison type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ base, then array elements: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ defaulted ==: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ declared return type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.spaceship]/2-4, [class.eq]/2-3, [class.compare.default]/6:
defaulted operator<=> and operator== compare the expanded list of
subobjects -- direct bases, then members, arrays element by element --
and an `auto' operator<=> returns the common comparison type of the
element comparisons (partial_ordering with a double member).  The front
end typed every defaulted <=> as int and compared only the members, an
array as a pointer (bin53).  defaulted_three_way_comparison builds the
body from xi <=> yi converted to R, and defaulted == uses the same
expanded list.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.
